{%- doc -%}
  The product title as a card should show it — without the suffix the badge is
  already saying.

  The publisher appends "— Front & Back" / "— Name & Number" to the title so
  the information survives the cart, the order confirmation email and search
  results, where a badge cannot follow it. On a product card the badge does say
  it, right on the image, so repeating it at the end of a title that wraps to
  three lines is noise.

  Only the exact suffix the badge is showing is removed, and only from the end.
  A product genuinely named something ending in those words keeps its name, and
  nothing anywhere else is affected — this changes one line of display text.

  @param {object} product - The product object.
  @param {string} badge - The label the card is already showing, or empty.

  @example
  {%- capture card_title -%}{%- render 'pro-listing-title', product: p, badge: pro_extra -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign shown = product.title

  if badge != blank
    assign em_dash_suffix = ' — ' | append: badge
    assign hyphen_suffix = ' - ' | append: badge

    if shown contains em_dash_suffix
      assign shown = shown | split: em_dash_suffix | first
    elsif shown contains hyphen_suffix
      assign shown = shown | split: hyphen_suffix | first
    endif
  endif

  echo shown | strip
-%}
